---
import { getImage } from 'astro:assets';
import libraryImage from '../../../src/assets/img/pexels-mehmetakifarts-37330363.webp';

const zinInputs = await getImage({ src: libraryImage, format: 'webp', quality: 85 });
---
<!-- ============================================================
       WHY A LIBRARY — NOT JUST NOTES
  ============================================================ -->
<section class="sec sec-tint" id="why-need-library">
  <div class="container sec-white p-4 rounded-3 shadow">

    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-12 col-md-4">

        <img
          src={libraryImage.src}
          alt="Zin — why a library - libraries compound"
          class="solution-img"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />

      </div>
      <div class="col-md-8 ps-2">

        <span class="zin-eyebrow">Why a library</span>
        <h2 class="zin-h2 mb-3">Notes capture. Libraries compound.</h2>

        <p class="zin-body mb-3">
          <b>A note sits on its own.</b> 
          <br />
          It holds a single thought, unconnected to anything else you have written, and it stays exactly as valuable as the day you wrote it.
        </p>

        <p class="zin-body mb-3">
          <b>A library accumulates.</b> 
          <br />
          Ideas gather across time and start to relate to each other. You read through a topic and a thought from three months ago meets something you captured yesterday, and together they produce something neither could have made alone.
        </p>

        <p class="zin-body mb-0">
          <b>That is the difference.</b> 
          <br />
          A note is worth what it says. A library is worth what it connects, and the longer it runs, the more it is worth.
        </p>

      </div>
      
    </div>

  </div>
</section>